    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0566" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg468"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 722.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Robert J. Thompson, of Chicago, who is
                    secretary of the Lafayette Memorial Commission, has been appointed by the
                    President a special commissioner to present to the President of the French
                    Republic the first Lafayette coin of a series of $50,000 authorized by Congress
                    in aid of the Lafayette memorial statue.</p>
                <p>The President will be pleased if you will make an appointment with His Excellency
                    President Loubet to present Mr. Thompson and to allow him the privilege of
                    presenting this coin in a silver casket especially designed for the purpose.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
